Yesterday the Investment Committee approved IC-2025-019 by a 7-0 vote, adding=
 the Cybersecurity Leaders Fund to the Growth models at a 4% weight. The allo=
cation is funded from the Global Technology Fund, which goes from 16% to 12% =
of the Growth model, so total technology exposure is essentially unchanged - =
we are shifting part of it toward dedicated security names.

Implementation: our trading desk will rebalance the 15 Growth taxable account=
s November 17-26. Please review the tax impact of the Global Technology Fund =
sale with each client before the trade date, and flag any client restriction =
on selling the fund to me and the desk by end of day today.

Talking points:
- Platform consolidation: enterprises are cutting the number of security vend=
ors they use, and we think scaled platforms such as CrowdStrike and Palo Alto=
 Networks are best placed to win those consolidated budgets.
- Zero trust: the shift to zero trust architectures and cloud security keeps =
security budgets resilient even when broader IT spending is under pressure.
- Complement, not duplicate: the Cybersecurity Leaders Fund is concentrated i=
n security platform leaders, while the Global Technology Fund owns them only =
at small weights.
- Risks: valuations across the group are full and competition is intense; thi=
s is a long-term position, not a trade.

The full thesis is in my November 3 note, "Cybersecurity Platform Consolidati=
on". Olivia Grant and I are happy to join client calls.

